  "chapter": {
    "number": 57,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(58) For the end. Destroy not: by David, for a memorial."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "If you⌃ do indeed speak righteousness, then do you⌃ judge rightly, you⌃ sons of men.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For you⌃ work iniquities in your hearts in the earth: your hands plot unrighteousness.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Sinners have gone astray from the womb: they go astray from the belly: they speak lies.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Their venom is like that of a serpent; as that of a deaf asp, and that stops her ears;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "which will not hear the voice of charmers, nor heed the",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 104
          },
          {
            "text": "charm prepared skillfully by the wise.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "God has crushed their teeth in their mouth: God has broken the cheek-teeth of the lions.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They shall utterly pass away like water running through: he shall bend his bow till they shall fail.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They shall be destroyed as melted wax: the fire has fallen and they have not seen the sun.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Before your thorns feel the white thorn, he shall swallow you up as living, as in his wrath.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The righteous shall rejoice when he sees the vengeance of the ungodly: he shall wash his hands in the blood of the sinner.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And a man shall say, Verily then there is",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 105
          },
          {
            "text": "a reward for the righteous: verily there is a God that judges them in the earth.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
